WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.760
From 1994, cheap Dyclofanac cut India's vultures by 97% or more and added over 100,000 deaths yearly. This is unintended consequences, episode 151. A pain killer meant for working cattle, a scavenger collapsed, nobody measured, a sanitation gap that reached people, a ban that leaked, and the test that was never required. Dyclofanac began as a human drug. In the 1970s, it was developed as a non-sterroidal anti-inflammatory for

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.700
arthritis and for pain after surgery. It did what that class of drugs is built to do.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:40.320
It eases swelling. It gave people back ordinary movement. When the patent lapsed in the early

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:46.540
1990s, Indian pharmaceutical firms made inexpensive versions. Farmers could finally afford a dose.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.060
Before that shift, livestock owners had few practical options for the pain and inflammation that

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:58.220
cut milk yields and draft power in working animals. A bullock that could not plow was not only an animal

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:03.440
and distress. It was a season of field work at risk. The drug therefore looked like a straight

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:08.360
forward welfare gain and a productivity gain for millions of small holders who had watched

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:13.160
cattle suffer without treatment. No one at the time tested the compound on the obligate

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:18.240
scavengers that cleaned the countryside of dead livestock. That omission was not a secret plot,

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:23.780
it was a blank in the file. In the absence of any published data on avian kidney physiology,

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:28.940
the decision carried no visible downside for the people who made the drug or administered it.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:33.720
Farmers in the Gangectic Plain and in Rajasthan, where cattle densities were highest,

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.600
saw immediate improvements in animal mobility after a single low-cost injection.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:45.600
The same dose that ease joint swelling in a bullock also kept the animal productive for another season of plowing or hauling.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:51.060
Because Diclofanac was already approved for human use, regulators treated the extension

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:55.520
to livestock as a minor administrative step rather than a new environmental release.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.260
The economic logic was simple arithmetic.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:03.080
One vile treated several animals at a fraction of the price of imported alternatives.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:07.240
Milk output or fieldwork could resume within days instead of weeks.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:12.480
For a small holder counting days until the next milking or the next planting, that arithmetic

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.900
was hard to argue with.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.920
The intended patient was the cow.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.420
The intended return was work and milk.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:22.200
Both of those showed up quickly, and both of those were easy to see.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:27.520
By the mid-1990s, veterinary use had spread rapidly through the cattle belt of northern

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:28.640
and western India.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:34.220
Roadside pharmacies and livestock markets stocked the human formulation in vials labeled for

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:34.580
cattle.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:38.740
Farmers injected animals shortly before slaughter or natural death.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:44.420
Early surveys by the Bombay Natural History Society recorded no obvious change in carcass

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:44.920
availability.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.980
Vultures still arrived in large numbers at known feeding sites.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:53.720
If you were standing at one of those sites in those years, the old picture still held.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:54.840
Birds came.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:55.940
Carcasses went.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:01.400
A few ornithologists noted occasional dead birds with white urate deposits around the vent.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:06.300
Those incidents were treated as isolated disease events rather than a systemic threat.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:11.760
that. That reading was available from the evidence then in hand. A handful of dead birds against

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:17.260
flocks that still filled the sky did not yet look like a collapse. The scale of adoption can be

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:23.280
traced in pharmacy sales records. Once the molecule entered the generic market, annual production volumes

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:29.000
rose from laboratory quantities to hundreds of tons. That was enough to dose millions of cattle each

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:34.720
year across states where open grazing was the norm. Because the human and veterinary supply chains were

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:39.780
not yet separated by regulation, the same blister packs moved from urban hospitals to

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:45.000
rural veterinary shops with minimal friction. A drug approved for people did not have to change

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:50.780
plants or packaging logic or much of its root to reach a bullock. Early monitoring focused on

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:56.520
whether the drug reduced clinical signs in livestock, no parallel program tracked residue levels in

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:01.880
the carcasses those livestock left behind. The first systematic neckropsees that later linked

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:06.960
the drug to vulture mortality were still years away, so the absence of reported problems

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:12.400
was taken as evidence of safety. Silence in the data was read as a clean result. It

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:17.620
was, more precisely, a result no one had yet gone looking for. The causal chain began

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:22.260
when a treated animal died and its carcass retained enough dichlephanic residue to kill

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:27.380
any vulture that fed on it. The bird did not have to receive an injection. It only had

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:32.640
to do the work it had always done. In 2004, J. Lindsey Oaks and colleagues published

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:37.620
in Nature the experimental proof. Oral doses matching those found in treated livestock

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:42.940
produced the visceral gout and kidney failure already seen in field carcasses. The white

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:48.440
deposits ornithologist had noted years earlier were not a scattered disease. They were a signature

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:54.620
of the drug. By 2007, the Oriental Whitebacked Vulture had declined to one-tenth of one percent

00:04:54.620 --> 00:05:00.780
of its early 1990s numbers, according to repeated road transect surveys reported in PLS-1.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:08.240
A 97% drop recorded between the early 1990s and 2007 left two few birds to process

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:14.240
the daily volume of livestock mortality across the subcontinent. Three GIPs species that had once

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:18.980
numbered in the tens of millions were within a decade of the generic flood are remnant.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:23.560
The arithmetic of exposure is straightforward once the residue data are examined.

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:27.920
A single-treated buffalo could contain several lethal doses for a vulture.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.620
Gip species feeding groups of dozens.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:35.480
One contaminated carcass could remove multiple breeding adults in a single afternoon.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.980
Without those adults returning to nests, recruitment collapsed.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:41.720
The loss was not only of birds in the air.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:45.000
It was of the next generation that those birds would have raised.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:50.560
With the primary scavengers gone, the carcasses that once disappeared within hours lay rotting

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:56.300
for days at village dumps and urban waste sites. That persistence was the first visible rearrangement

00:05:56.300 --> 00:06:01.800
of the countryside. Feral dog populations rose sharply, because an abundant, previously

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:06.900
contested food source was now uncontested. Each additional dog raised the probability

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:12.460
of a human bite. India already accounted for roughly a third of global rabies deaths, so

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:16.620
the bite risk landed on a country that was already carrying a heavy share of that disease.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:22.520
At the same time, uneaten carcasses leached pathogens into shallow aquifers and streams used

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.660
for washing and irrigation.

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:27.980
Surface water near carcass dumps showed elevated bacterial loads.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:33.300
The effect concentrated in the same districts that had once supported the densest vulture colonies.

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:39.320
The sanitation gap therefore ran through two measurable pathways, more dogs and dirtier

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:42.240
water in the places where the birds had been thickest.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:47.840
Economists, A.L. Frank and Anant Sudarshan used the natural experiment of districts that

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.680
historically differed in vulture habitat suitability.

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:57.320
In the American Economic Review, they estimated that all cause human mortality rose 4.7% in

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:00.740
high suitability districts between 2000 and 2005.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:06.160
Districts that had supported the largest vulture populations recorded human death rates more than

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:10.200
4% higher than comparable districts that had never hosted many vultures.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:20.040
The 4.7% increase reflects both direct zoonotic risk and the broader degradation of local water quality once the keystone scavenger was removed.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:28.500
A narrow approval for a cattle painkiller had, through residue, kidney failure and an emptied sky, become a public health number.

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:34.620
India banned veterinary dichofanac in 2006 and strengthened the prohibition in 2008.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:40.480
The response was real, it was also late relative to the collapse already measured, and it had

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:42.840
to work through supply chains that had already mixed.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:49.320
Follow-up Carcass surveys published in PLOS-1 showed the prevalence of dicholophanec contaminated

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:55.520
livestock fell from roughly 10.8% before the ban to 6.5% several years later.

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:59.160
That fall slowed the declines, it did not stop them.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:06.300
Nicaropsies of Vultures found dead between 2008 and 2012, reported in Oryx, revealed that

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:11.640
some birds still carried Dyclophannac, others showed Nymusulide residues associated with

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:13.020
the same gout pathology.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:17.860
Human formulation Dyclophannac continues to be diverted into veterinary channels.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:23.920
Populations of the three-gip species remain at a few percent of pre-1990s levels, with

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:25.460
only modest signs of recovery.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:30.340
The persistence of the drug after the formal ban illustrates the difficulty of separating

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:35.440
two parallel supply chains that share the same molecule and the same manufacturing plants.

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:41.620
Even after the 2008 tightening, which required colored dyes and larger vial sizes for human

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:45.740
formulations, enforcement relied on state-level pharmacy inspections.

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:49.340
Those inspections could not monitor every rural transaction.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.880
A dye and a bigger vial are signals.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.680
They are not a seal on every roadside shop.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:09:01.580
Meanwhile, alternative non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, such as Nemisolide, entered the veterinary

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:05.880
market without the same level of pre-release testing against vulture kidney tissue.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:09.640
The original oversight was reproduced at a smaller scale.

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:11.500
The band changed the label.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:13.020
It did not, by itself.

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:17.000
Change the question regulators had failed to ask in 1994.

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:23.640
When regulators approved Diclofan Act for livestock, they evaluated only the intended patient species

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:26.080
and the immediate economic return to farmers.

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:30.580
The process rewarded any low-cost drug that cleared livestock quickly.

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:36.780
It did not require tests on the scavengers whose removal would later impose sanitation costs in human lives.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:39.480
A second principle sits beside that one.

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:46.900
Once a compound enters widespread agricultural use, a later ban on the veterinary formulation can still be undermined

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:51.780
by leakage from the parallel human supply chain that regulators continue to authorize.

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:57.320
The burden that was missing is a demonstration of safety for the entire local scavenger community

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:59.000
before marketing approval.

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:03.980
That requirement would move the proof from post-release mortality counts to pre-release

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:04.660
feeding trials.

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:10.820
If you follow how an ecological loss shows up inside human death rates, environmental intelligence

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:13.480
on the Narrow Network stays with that kind of measurement.

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:18.620
The same narrow gate still opens whenever a livestock medicine is cleared on how fast

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:19.820
to herd returns to work.

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:25.580
work. If a new anti-inflammatory or antibiotic is approved for cattle on productivity data alone,

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:30.420
what would you look for in the file? A feeding trial on the animals that eat the dead,

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:35.940
or only a note that the cow stood up sooner? That's the case for today. The lessons tend

